  "description": "The 2026 election for Massachusetts's 8th Congressional District will be held on November 3, 2026, with the Democratic and Republican primaries scheduled for September 1, 2026. The district covers parts of Boston and its southern suburbs, including Quincy, Brockton, and Weymouth, and has a Cook PVI of D+15, making it a safely Democratic seat. Incumbent Democrat Stephen Lynch, first elected in 2001, faces a primary challenge from attorney and voting rights advocate Patrick Roath, who argues for new leadership and more progressive policies. The Republican primary features Walter Grochowski, though the general election is widely expected to remain in Democratic hands.",
